# Patch TWRP for afyonlte (Renesas)



Due to the obvious quirkiness and lack of documentation for the Renesas MP5232 chipset, the framebuffer on TWRP will not work out of the box.

Some patching is required to get a stable image on the screen.

In `bootable/recovery/minuitwrp/graphics_fbdev.cpp`, find this block of code:

```cpp
static void set_displayed_framebuffer(unsigned n)
{
    if (n > 1 || !double_buffered) return;

    vi.yres_virtual = gr_framebuffer[0].height * 2;
    vi.yoffset = n * gr_framebuffer[0].height;
    vi.bits_per_pixel = gr_framebuffer[0].pixel_bytes * 8;
```

Patch it so that it looks like this:

```cpp
static void set_displayed_framebuffer(unsigned n)
{
    if (n > 1 || !double_buffered) return;

    vi.yres_virtual = gr_framebuffer[0].height; // * 2
    vi.yoffset = 960; //n * gr_framebuffer[0].height;
    vi.bits_per_pixel = gr_framebuffer[0].pixel_bytes * 8;
```

(28/05/2026) I've had some issues with getting ro.hardware property set properly, so the get the `mpro` helper service working (defined in `init.recovery.u2.rc`), patch your `bootable/recovery/etc/init.rc` imports on the top to look like this:

```
import /init.recovery.logd.rc
import /init.recovery.usb.rc
import /init.recovery.u2.rc
```

So instead of `/init.recovery.$(ro.hardware).rc`, `/init.recovery.u2.rc` is used.
